1
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:54,000
The Mountain Men is a adventure, western, drama film directed by Richard Lang.

2
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:42,000
The story concerns two grizzled mountain men -- Bill Tyler and Henry
Frapp -- during the dying days of the fur-trapping era.

3
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:30,000
The plot begins when Running Moon runs away from her abusive husband
Heavy Eagle and comes across the two seedy fur trappers.

4
00:27:12,000 --> 00:27:18,000
The mountain men take her in, unaware that Heavy Eagle has
dispatched an army of Indian braves to reclaim her.

5
00:34:00,000 --> 00:34:06,000
Bill Tyler, played by Charlton Heston.

6
00:40:48,000 --> 00:40:54,000
Henry Frapp, played by Brian Keith.

7
00:47:36,000 --> 00:47:42,000
Running Moon, played by Victoria Racimo.

8
00:54:24,000 --> 00:54:30,000
Heavy Eagle, played by Stephen Macht.

9
01:01:12,000 --> 01:01:18,000
La Bont, played by Seymour Cassel.

10
01:08:00,000 --> 01:08:06,000
Medicine Wolf, played by David Ackroyd.

11
01:14:48,000 --> 01:14:54,000
The Mountain Men is a 1980 American adventure Western film directed by
Richard Lang and starring Charlton Heston and Brian Keith.

12
01:21:36,000 --> 01:21:42,000
Heston's son, Fraser Clarke Heston, wrote the screenplay.

13
01:28:24,000 --> 01:28:30,000
The film explores themes of native american, frontier,
frontier justice, 19th century, mountain man.

14
01:35:12,000 --> 01:35:18,000
The tone is emotional.
